## Failed sweep before the fix (preserved)

Two earlier runs of the same committed recipe with a fixed DRAIN=28
(`/tmp/w180-try`, `/tmp/w178-lgp`) aborted at `malloc(): corrupted top size`
before any `gp_camera_file_get`. A manual sweep in `/tmp/w178-lgp` showed
DRAIN 24..29 corrupt, 30..32 disclose the canary; a fixed DRAIN=30 then
failed under a second clean archive (`/tmp/w180-clean-build`). The criterion
is the victim chunk at `priv+0x4050`, not a numeric drain, so the script now
sweeps DRAIN 20..40 and records the selected value. This is a layout
calibration, not a new claim: the reported disclosure, control behaviour and
grade are unchanged.

## Limits (unchanged)

Author replay of committed files plus the pinned release tarball; not an
independent witness verdict. The disclosure goes to a HOST consumer through
the real public API; W176 still holds — this camlib never echoes table bytes
to the device, so a malicious camera cannot read the canary or pointers this
way. No wire path, device-only canary recovery, pointer dereference without
gdb, command or rung 5. Rung 5 UNKNOWN.
